+        <h2 id="opa-g-title">OPA-G · Open Photonic Graphics Accelerator</h2>
+        <p>OPA-G investigates whether photonics can reduce the energy and latency of graphics workloads. The first target is the ray–box test in a bounding volume hierarchy (BVH). Over time, the research will examine hybrid ray tracing, stereoscopic VR and real-time rendering of AI-generated 3D worlds. The electronic renderer initially handles traversal, triangle tests, shading, textures and display.</p>
+        <p><a href="#photonic-circuit-lab/ray-tracing">Try Chip 16 · Photonic Ray Tracing Accelerator</a></p>
+        <table class="data-table">
+          <caption>Seven research phases</caption>
+          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Phase</th><th scope="col">Deliverable and validation</th></tr></thead>
+          <tbody>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPA-G-001</th><td>Numerical baseline. Establish forward ray–AABB ground truth, test geometric edge cases independently and publish seeded precision sweeps with separate false-positive and false-negative counts.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPA-G-002</th><td>Reconstruct the published side-function algorithm from its supplementary derivation and compare its 3D conventions and edge cases with G-001.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPA-G-003</th><td>Model four Mach–Zehnder modulators and coherent readout. Sweep bias, nonlinearity, loss, phase drift, noise and comparator thresholds with calibrated uncertainty.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPA-G-004</th><td>Compare matched CPU and GPU workloads. Report throughput, p50/p95 latency and energy per correct test, including memory and conversion overhead, laser power and idle power.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPA-G-005</th><td>Design a process-specific test coupon with RF and optical interfaces and reference structures. Verify process access, model validity and foundry design rules before fabrication.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPA-G-006</th><td>Measure the test chip at calibrated electrical and optical reference planes. Publish raw traces, uncertainty, drift and error counts against the same reference.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPA-G-007</th><td>Integrate a hybrid GPU/FPGA path with conservative fallback. Measure image errors, frame timing and whole-system energy before OPVR integration.</td></tr>
+          </tbody>
+        </table>
+        <p><a href="https://github.com/cryptomanxxx/debatt-ai-open-photonic-lab/blob/main/research/OPA-G-ROADMAP.md">Read the OPA-G research plan</a></p>
+      </section>
