+            <tr><th scope="row">OPVR-001</th><td>Open system specification and electronic baseline. Set resolution, 72/90/120 Hz profiles, tracking measurements, thermal limits and battery budgets.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPVR-002</th><td>Chip 16 teaching demo and OPA-G-001 numerical baseline with independently checked reference cases.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPVR-003</th><td>OPA-G optical model and end-to-end accounting at matched graphics quality.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPVR-004</th><td>Process-qualified external test chip and calibrated bench verification, subject to access and funding.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPVR-005</th><td>GPU/FPGA integration with measurements of data movement and frame-time tails.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPVR-006</th><td>Tethered headset with external accelerator. Compare identical scenes and render settings, dropped frames and motion-to-photon latency.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPVR-007</th><td>Assess packaging, heat, mass, battery, electrical and optical safety, EMC and reliability. Obtain independent safety review before wearable laser prototyping.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPVR-008</th><td>Standalone hybrid prototype after passing system energy, thermal, safety and latency gates.</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">OPVR-009</th><td>Open distribution prototype with documented APIs, optional agent integration, security review and a device compatibility matrix. This work can proceed independently of the optical hardware.</td></tr>
+          </tbody>
+        </table>
